**EXCERPT FROM MANUFACTURING AND SUPPLY AGREEMENT**

**THIS MANUFACTURING AND SUPPLY AGREEMENT (the "Agreement") is made and entered into as of the 1st day of January, 2024 (the "Effective Date"), by and between:**

**1. ABC Manufacturing, Inc.**  
a corporation duly organized and existing under the laws of the State of California, with its principal place of business located at 1000 Industrial Way, Los Angeles, California 90001, hereinafter referred to as "Manufacturer,"  

**AND**

**2. XYZ Electronics Corp.**  
a corporation duly organized and existing under the laws of the State of New York, with its principal place of business located at 2000 Tech Park, New York, New York 10001, hereinafter referred to as "Client."  

**WHEREAS**, the Manufacturer is engaged in the business of manufacturing electronic components and has the necessary facilities, equipment, and expertise to produce components suitable for the Client's specifications;  

**WHEREAS**, the Client desires to procure certain electronic components from the Manufacturer and has agreed to the terms and conditions set forth herein;  

**NOW, THEREFORE**, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements contained herein, the parties hereby agree as follows:

---

**ARTICLE I: PRODUCT SPECIFICATIONS AND MANUFACTURING PROCESS**

1.1 **Product Specifications**  
The Manufacturer shall produce the following products (the "Products") in accordance with the specifications outlined in Exhibit A attached hereto and incorporated herein by reference:  
   a. Model No. XJ-45 Microprocessor  
   b. Model No. QK-21 Sensor Module  
   c. Model No. RT-88 Power Supply Unit  

1.2 **Manufacturing Process**  
The manufacturing process for the Products shall include the following stages:  
   a. Sourcing of raw materials from approved suppliers, including but not limited to Silicon Valley Components LLC, located at 1500 Circuit Road, San Jose, California 95112.  
   b. Assembly on production line #3 at the Manufacturer’s facility, which is equipped with state-of-the-art robotic arms and automated testing stations.  
   c. Quality control inspections conducted by the Manufacturer’s Quality Assurance Department, overseen by Ms. Jennifer Lee, Quality Control Manager, who shall report directly to Mr. Thomas Brown, Chief Operations Officer.

---

**ARTICLE II: QUALITY CONTROL AND INSPECTION**

2.1 **Quality Control Standards**  
The Manufacturer shall adhere to ISO 9001:2015 quality management standards throughout the production process. All Products are required to meet the specifications set forth in Exhibit A, which includes tolerances, performance metrics, and safety compliance parameters.

2.2 **Inspection Procedures**  
   a. Initial Inspection: A pre-production sample of each Product shall be submitted to the Client for approval prior to the commencement of mass production.  
   b. Ongoing Inspection: The Manufacturer shall conduct in-process inspections at regular intervals during manufacturing, with records maintained and made available to the Client upon request.  
   c. Final Inspection: Upon completion of production, the Manufacturer shall provide a final inspection report to the Client, detailing compliance with all specifications.

---

**ARTICLE III: DELIVERY AND ACCEPTANCE**

3.1 **Delivery Schedule**  
The Manufacturer agrees to deliver the Products in accordance with the following schedule:  
   a. Initial Shipment: 10,000 units of Model No. XJ-45 Microprocessor by March 31, 2024.  
   b. Subsequent Shipments: Monthly shipments of 5,000 units per model thereafter, with the final shipment to be completed by December 31, 2024.

3.2 **Acceptance Criteria**  
   a. The Client shall have seven (7) business days from the date of delivery to inspect the Products and provide written notice to the Manufacturer of any non-conformity.  
   b. If no written notice is received within the specified period, the Products shall be deemed accepted.

---

**ARTICLE IV: PRICING AND PAYMENT TERMS**

4.1 **Pricing Structure**  
The pricing for the Products shall be as follows:  
   a. Model No. XJ-45 Microprocessor: $10.00 per unit  
   b. Model No. QK-21 Sensor Module: $15.00 per unit  
   c. Model No. RT-88 Power Supply Unit: $12.00 per unit  

4.2 **Payment Terms**  
   a. An initial deposit of 30% of the total estimated cost shall be due upon execution of this Agreement.  
   b. The remaining balance shall be payable within thirty (30) days following the acceptance of each shipment.

---

**ARTICLE V: WARRANTIES AND LIABILITY**

5.1 **Manufacturer Warranties**  
The Manufacturer warrants that the Products shall be free from defects in materials and workmanship for a period of twelve (12) months from the date of acceptance. The Manufacturer's sole obligation under this warranty shall be to repair or replace any defective Products, provided that the Client notifies the Manufacturer in writing within the warranty period.

5.2 **Limitation of Liability**  
In no event shall either party be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from or related to this Agreement, including but not limited to loss of profits or business interruption.

---

**ARTICLE VI: CONFIDENTIALITY AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY**

6.1 **Confidentiality Obligations**  
Both parties agree to maintain the confidentiality of the proprietary information exchanged in connection with this Agreement. Confidential information shall not be disclosed to any third party without the prior written consent of the disclosing party.

6.2 **Intellectual Property Rights**  
All intellectual property rights arising from the manufacturing of the Products shall be retained by the Manufacturer. However, the Client shall have a non-exclusive, perpetual license to use the specifications and designs provided for the duration of this Agreement.

---

**ARTICLE VII: TERMINATION**

7.1 **Termination for Convenience**  
Either party may terminate this Agreement for any reason upon thirty (30) days' written notice to the other party.

7.2 **Termination for Cause**  
Either party may terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice if the other party fails to perform any material obligation under this Agreement and such failure is not cured within fifteen (15) days after receipt of notice of such failure.

---

**ARTICLE VIII: MISCELLANEOUS**

8.1 **Governing Law**  
This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of California.

8.2 **Dispute Resolution**  
Any disputes arising out of or related to this Agreement shall be resolved through arbitration in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association, with the venue to be in Los Angeles, California.

8.3 **Entire Agreement**  
This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding between the parties and supersedes all prior discussions and agreements, whether written or oral, relating to the subject matter hereof.

---

